   "stem": {
      "text": "A particle moves along a line, and its position \\( s(t) \\) satisfies the differential equation \\( \\frac{ds}{dt} = 3 t^{2} - 4 t + 1 \\) with \\( s(0) = 5 \\). Writing the particular solution as \\( s(t) = 5 + \\int_{0}^{t} v(u) \\, du \\), where \\( v \\) is the given rate, find the exact value of \\( s(2) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 7
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The accumulation form of the solution is \\( s(t) = 5 + \\int_{0}^{t} v(u) \\, du \\), with an antiderivative of the rate \\( t^{3} - 2 t^{2} + t \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Power",
               "t",
               3
            ],
            [
               "Negate",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  2,
                  [
                     "Power",
                     "t",
                     2
                  ]
               ]
            ],
            "t"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The initial value fixes the constant term: at \\( t = 0 \\) the integral is 0, so \\( s(0) = 5 \\).",
         "mathjson": 5
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Evaluate the integral: \\( \\int_{0}^{2} v(u) \\, du = 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( s(2) = 5 + 2 = 7 \\).",
         "mathjson": 7
      }
   ],
